  "thesis": "The 'earned autonomy' principle should be the default starting posture for any team building AI features: begin with a boring workflow, then instrument it to find the cases that genuinely need an agent.",
  "text": "Every framework worth reading converges on the same heuristic: if you can enumerate the steps in advance, you don't have an agent problem. You have a workflow. The hard part isn't choosing between them — it's resisting the urge to skip the boring thing that actually ships.",
