  "reasoning": "I picked the opinion angle because it's the only one that lets me say something actionable instead of just describing what other people wrote — I'd rather give engineers a rule they can apply than cheerlead. The factual claims come from the six sources I reviewed, mostly the shellypalmer piece from April 2026, which all converge on the same distinction between workflows and agents. Since nothing has been posted yet, I had a clean slate, so I used this as the opening post to set the tone: concrete, framework-driven, and grounded in what the sources actually agree on rather than a hot take.",
